Imports:
  - Types:
      - TSAccountManager
    From: SignalServiceKit/Account/TSAccountManager
  - Types:
      - SDSDatabaseStorage
    From: SignalServiceKit/Storage/Database/SDSDatabaseStorage
  - Types:
      - ThreadStore
      - ThreadDeletionManager
    From: SignalServiceKit/Threads
  - Types:
      - GroupsV2
      - GroupManager
    From: SignalServiceKit/Groups
  - Types:
      - InteractionStore
      - InteractionDeleteManager
    From: SignalServiceKit/Messages/Interactions
  - Types:
      - MessageSender
    From: SignalServiceKit/Messages

Usages:
  composition_root: |
    Every manager/store/service instance is constructed exactly once, by hand, in a fixed
    dependency order during app launch, before this cell's own instance is constructed from
    the full set of already-built instances. This cell holds no construction logic of its
    own — it is a plain aggregate published once and read thereafter as a shared instance.
  migration_bridge: |
    This is explicitly a transitional composition root: newer, protocol-based code obtains
    its dependencies from this cell's properties instead of the legacy global-accessor
    pattern it is gradually superseding. It is not intended to be the permanent shape of
    dependency wiring.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the app's composition root for its modern, protocol-based managers and
  stores: it exposes one already-constructed instance of nearly every subsystem documented
  elsewhere in this forest, so any code can obtain its dependencies from one shared place
  instead of constructing or looking them up itself.
  Use `composition_root` for how and when this cell's single type is populated.
  Use `migration_bridge` for why this cell exists at all.

---

"DependenciesBridge()":
  location: DependenciesBridge.swift
  annotations: |
    The app's composition-root aggregate, published once at launch and read thereafter as a
    shared instance.

    Use `composition_root` for construction/publication timing.
    Use `migration_bridge` for this type's overall purpose.
    Use `TSAccountManager`, `SDSDatabaseStorage`, `ThreadStore`, `ThreadDeletionManager`,
    `GroupsV2`, `GroupManager`, `InteractionStore`, `InteractionDeleteManager`, and
    `MessageSender` from Imports as the subsystem instances this aggregate exposes.
  properties:
    "tsAccountManager -> TSAccountManager": |
      The shared local account/registration state manager.
    "db -> SDSDatabaseStorage": |
      The shared database transaction facade.
    "threadStore -> ThreadStore": |
      The shared thread data-access instance.
    "threadDeletionManager -> ThreadDeletionManager": |
      The shared thread deletion coordinator.
    "interactionStore -> InteractionStore": |
      The shared interaction data-access instance.
    "interactionDeleteManager -> InteractionDeleteManager": |
      The shared interaction deletion coordinator.
    "messageSender -> MessageSender": |
      The shared outgoing-message send entry point.
  methods:
    "setShared(dependenciesBridge: String)": |
      Publishes the fully constructed aggregate as the app-wide shared instance.

      Algorithm:
      1. Assert this has not already been published outside of test runs, per `composition_root`.
      2. Store the given instance as the shared instance readable via this cell's static accessor.

